** Regression test for the inexactnewton linear solver (lagged-LU-preconditioned GMRES with
** Eisenstat-Walker forcing). Same finite-strain plasticity cantilever as
** CantileverBeamQuad8NeoHookeWaPlastic -- several Newton iterations per increment, so the
** preconditioner-reuse path is genuinely exercised -- solved with linsolver=inexactnewton.
**
** The SuperLU delegate is chosen deliberately so the test is dependency-free and runs wherever the
** edelweiss-only suite runs; the production delegate is PARDISO (see the linsolver docs). The
** converged solution is independent of the linear solver, so U.ref matches a direct solve to well
** within the suite's 1e-6 tolerance.
*material, name=neohookewaplastic, id=neohookewaplastic, provider=edelweiss
91304.34783, 100000., 260, 70, 320, 9

*section, name=section1, thickness=40.0, material=neohookewaplastic, type=plane
all

*job, name=cps4job, domain=2d
*solver, solver=NIST, name=theSolver
linsolver=inexactnewton
linsolverConfigFile=inexactnewton.json

*fieldOutput
>>perNode, nSet=gen_bottom, result=P, field=displacement, name=RF
>>perNode, elSet=all, field=displacement, result=U, name=displacement

*modelGenerator, generator=planeRectQuad, name=gen
x0=0, l=1000
y0=0, h=100
elType=CPE8TL
elProvider=edelweiss
nX=20
nY=2

*output, type=monitor
fieldOutput=RF, f(x)='mean(x[:,1])'

*step, solver=theSolver
maxInc=1e-0, minInc=1e-8, maxNumInc=1000, maxIter=25, stepLength=100
>>dirichlet, name=left, nSet=gen_left,  field=displacement, 2=0, 1=0
>>nodeforces, name=cloadTop, nSet=gen_rightTop, components='0,-25000', field=displacement
